<title>USA: Ford, Pepsi, DuPont spin-offs possible? - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Ford, Pepsi, DuPont spin-offs possible? - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Will Ford Motor Co, PepsiCo Inc, and DuPont Co follow big blue chips such as AT&amp;T Corp and Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp by spinning off large pieces of their respective businesses in the near future? asks Andrew Bary in the September 23 issue of Barron's.</p>
<p>Bary notes that &quot;spin-offs remain a popular way for corporate managers to showcase fast-growing businesses, dump losers, separate extraneous operations and placate angry institutional shareholders who want something done about a weak stock price.&quot;</p>
